{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-10-Nov-2022-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The ratio of the number of boys to that of girls in a school is 5 : 2. If 87% of the boys and 80% of the girls passed in the annual exams, then find the percentage of students who failed in the annual exams.", "options": [{"text": "18%", "added": false}, {"text": "16%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}, {"text": "17%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "Aarush and Maahi together can do a piece of work in 10 days. If Aarush alone can do the same work in 15 days, then how many days Maahi alone will take to do the same work?", "options": [{"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Swati sold a bag to Ankita at a gain of 15%. Aashi bought this bag from Ankita for Rs.24,840. Ankita earned a profit of 20%. At what price would Swati have bought the bag?", "options": [{"text": "Rs.18,500", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.18,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.16,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.20,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5295", "added": false}, {"text": "5300", "added": false}, {"text": "5307", "added": false}, {"text": "5315", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "D", "added": false}, {"text": "A", "added": false}, {"text": "C", "added": false}, {"text": "B", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "Geeta runs 5/2 times as fast as Babita. In a race, if Geeta gives a lead of 40 m to Babita, find the distance from the starting point where both of them will meet (correct up to two decimal places).", "options": [{"text": "66.67 m", "added": false}, {"text": "65 m", "added": false}, {"text": "65.33 m", "added": false}, {"text": "66 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "In a showroom the price of a washing machine is ₹ 65,000. The customer gets cash discount of ₹ 2,000, and gets a scratch card promising percentage discount of 10% to 15%. Determine the difference between the least and the maximum selling prices of the washing machine.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "18.98 units", "added": false}, {"text": "23.58 units", "added": false}, {"text": "26.59 units", "added": false}, {"text": "21.62 units", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Two trains, running between Bangalore and Chennai, start at the same time from their respective locations and proceed towards each other at the speed of 80km/h and 95km/h. When they meet, it is found that one train has travelled 180km more than the other.The distance between Bangalore and Chennai is _______.", "options": [{"text": "1200 km", "added": false}, {"text": "2100 km", "added": false}, {"text": "345km", "added": false}, {"text": "400 km", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The simplified form of (7x + 4y)2 + (7x − 4y)2 is:", "options": [{"text": "98x2 + 32y2", "added": false}, {"text": "98x2 + 32y2 – 5xy", "added": false}, {"text": "32x2 + 98y2", "added": false}, {"text": "98x2 − 32y2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "A man bought two bicycles for ₹3,000 each. If he sells one bicycle at a profit of 10%, then for how much percentage profit should he sell the other bicycle so that he makes a profit of 20% on the whole?", "options": [{"text": "15 Percent", "added": false}, {"text": "25 Percent", "added": false}, {"text": "30 Percent", "added": false}, {"text": "10 Percent", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "Which of the following is the smallest ratio?", "options": [{"text": "41 : 92", "added": false}, {"text": "33 : 41", "added": false}, {"text": "42 : 49", "added": false}, {"text": "35 : 47", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "If a car covers 75.5 km in 3.5 litres of petrol, how much distance (in km) will it cover in 28 litres of petrol?", "options": [{"text": "603", "added": false}, {"text": "602", "added": false}, {"text": "604", "added": false}, {"text": "600", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "direct-inverse-variation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "Find the effective discount for the scheme – Buy 5 get 3 free.", "options": [{"text": "36.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "37.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "36%", "added": false}, {"text": "37%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "roots", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "A car travels with a speed of 21 m/sec in the first 10 minutes, 9.0 km in the next 10 minutes and 10 km in the last 10 minutes of its journey. What is the average speed of the car in km/h during its entire journey?", "options": [{"text": "60.0 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "63.2 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "62.0 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "65.3 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "The number 150328 is divisible by 23. If the digits are rearranged in descending order and five times of 13 is subtracted from the new number thus formed, then the resultant number will be divisible by:", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "What are the values of x and y, respectively, from the following equations? 6x + 7y = 5xy 10y – 4x = 4xy", "options": [{"text": "3 and 4", "added": false}, {"text": "4 and 5", "added": false}, {"text": "2 and 4", "added": false}, {"text": "2 and 5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Geography, Mathematics", "added": false}, {"text": "Science, Geography", "added": false}, {"text": "Science, English", "added": false}, {"text": "English, Mathematics", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 1", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "A car covered the first 100 km at a speed of 50 km/h. It covered next 140 km at a speed of 70 km/h. What is its average speed?", "options": [{"text": "60 km/ h", "added": false}, {"text": "62 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "58 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "64 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "What is the length of the longest pole that can fit itself in a hall 60 feet long, 30 feet broad and 20 feet high?", "options": [{"text": "50 feet", "added": false}, {"text": "70 feet", "added": false}, {"text": "30 feet", "added": false}, {"text": "20 feet", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Jan", "added": false}, {"text": "April", "added": false}, {"text": "May", "added": false}, {"text": "February", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "How many metallic spheres, each of diameter 6 cm can be melted to mould into a solid cylinder of diameter 8 cm and height of 18 cm?", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "Find the HCF of 238 and 832.", "options": [{"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "The volume of a wall, six times as high as its breadth and half as long as its height, is 23958 cm3. What is the breadth of the wall?", "options": [{"text": "21 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "15 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "11 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "18 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "frustum-prism-pyramid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "If Ram’s income exceeds Shyam’s income by 70% and Shyam’s income is less than Sohan’s income by 30%, then find the ratio of the incomes of Ram and Sohan.", "options": [{"text": "119 : 100", "added": false}, {"text": "121 : 102", "added": false}, {"text": "120 : 101", "added": false}, {"text": "118 : 99", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "What are the values of R and M, respectively, if the given number is perfectly divisible by 16 and 11 ? 34R05030M6", "options": [{"text": "4 and 6", "added": false}, {"text": "7 and 5", "added": false}, {"text": "5 and 5", "added": false}, {"text": "5 and 7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "If a 4 digit number x58y is exactly divisible by 9, then the least value of (x + y) is:", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "secθ", "added": false}, {"text": "sinθ", "added": false}, {"text": "cotθ", "added": false}, {"text": "tanθ", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "A sphere is of radius 5 cm. What is the surface area of the sphere?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1289.17", "added": false}, {"text": "1279.62", "added": false}, {"text": "1278.36", "added": false}, {"text": "1288.62", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1.16 million", "added": false}, {"text": "3.17 million", "added": false}, {"text": "1.87 million", "added": false}, {"text": "2.17 million", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "If x + y = 10, 2xy = 48 and x > y, then find 2x - y.", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "Two stations are 120 km apart on a straight line. A train starts from station A at 8 a.m. and moves towards station B at 20 km/h, and another train starts from station B at 9 a.m. and travels towards station A at a speed of 30 km/h. At what time will they meet?", "options": [{"text": "10:30 a.m.", "added": false}, {"text": "10:00 a.m.", "ad